      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=g^{6},\\,g=- 2 x^{4} - x^{3}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=6g^{5},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=- 8 x^{3} - 3 x^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=6g^{5}\\cdot (- 8 x^{3} - 3 x^{2}) \\\\  &=6(- 2 x^{4} - x^{3})^{5}(- 8 x^{3} - 3 x^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
